hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"938","Na, Bundar, Na, Muhammad, H. Abu Musa told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told me, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Al-Alaa speaking, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrating it on the authority of his Lord. He said: “I am the best of partners.” And Bundar said: “I am the richest.” Partners for polytheism. Whoever does a deed and associates others with it, then I am innocent of it, and it belongs to the one who associated it.” And Bundar said: He said: “So I am innocent of it.” And to seek his reward from Him.” And Pindar said: On the authority of Al-Ala."
